## Original Content
Une série d’opérations de déstabilisation, attribuées à des réseaux prorusses, ont visé plusieurs candidats à la présidentielle ces derniers mois, selon la France.

## Summary
Moscow has accused candidates in the French presidential election of baselessly invoking the Russian threat. France reports that pro-Russian networks have conducted destabilization operations against several candidates in recent months.

## Key Points
- Moscow accuses French presidential candidates of using the Russian threat without justification.
- France attributes destabilization operations to pro-Russian networks.
- These operations have targeted multiple candidates in the lead-up to the election.
- The situation highlights geopolitical tensions and potential foreign interference.


